@startuml
title Namespace placement and template-owned HTTPRoute (issue 84)
actor "PE / Developer" as User
participant "Console / Catalog" as Catalog
participant Planner
participant Provisioning
participant "Kubernetes API" as Kube
participant "Git Template" as Template
participant "CD / Inventory" as CD
User -> Catalog: Register namespace, Gateway and endpoint Definitions
Catalog -> Catalog: Validate references / no infrastructure writes
User -> Planner: Preview native or Score workload
Planner -> Planner: Resolve consumer -> namespace -> cluster
Planner -> Planner: Resolve endpoint -> Gateway -> cluster
Planner -> Planner: Require same cluster and route capability; pin policy
Planner --> User: Plan / no reservation or Kubernetes mutation
User -> Provisioning: Deploy reviewed plan
Provisioning -> Kube: Verify existing cluster API / readiness
Provisioning -> Provisioning: Echo Gateway metadata; verify pinned provenance
Provisioning -> Kube: Create owned namespace and database in dependency order
Provisioning -> Provisioning: Reserve hostname/path atomically
Provisioning -> Kube: Read listener readiness / allowed namespace
Provisioning -> Template: Authorized endpoint intent + workload inputs
Template --> Provisioning: Workload, Service and HTTPRoute manifests
Provisioning -> Provisioning: Validate route against intent and actual Service
Provisioning -> CD: Publish one workload inventory
CD -> Kube: Reconcile owned objects
User -> CD: Update / remove application
CD -> Kube: Prune owned HTTPRoute and workload objects
CD -> Provisioning: Acknowledged removal
Provisioning -> Provisioning: Release claims / cleanup owned DB and namespace
note over Kube: Shared Gateway, Traefik, DNS and TLS are never changed or destroyed
@enduml
